{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790987173,"nonce":"hIHn3I1MSzuIx1Zb+PII656GqtE=","title":"Text measurement ignores letter spacing","message":"TextMeasureContext (crates/blinc_layout/src/tree.rs) carries content, font size, line height, wrap, family, weight and italic, but not letter_spacing. RenderProps.letter_spacing is set by CSS letter-spacing and the builder, and drawn, but layout measures the text without it: a run with positive spacing overflows its box, and negative spacing leaves a gap. Found by ashui binding Tailwind-style tracking- classes: the letter spacing reaches the props but the laid-out width does not change. Expected: letter_spacing in TextMeasureContext, applied per glyph gap by the measurer (and in the text_measurer feature's measure).","files":null}]}